I was looking at the DRF results (the statistics and the plots), and it seems that usually if the estimated line and shaded error area go fully above or below 0.0 (but perhaps not both above and below), that there is significant signed DRF. I got this result for the attached plot. I see the unsigned DRF is significant, but I was wondering if you could help me interpret the signed DRF in relation to the plot. I have other examples where there is significant DRF for a similar plot and am happy to post them if that helps.

Perhaps I am oversimplifying things; I thought I had noticed this pattern about the plots, but I could easily be wrong. Thank you!

